    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-rated asset with a score of 83.29, benefiting from an favorable matchup against Keider Montero. His projections are bolstered by a robust 14% boost from dynamic platoon splits and a prime spot in the #3 hole. Alongside him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.51) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (74.47) offer elite upside. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives against the volatile Max Scherzer, while **Luis Robert Jr.** gains significant leverage from a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez. We are prioritizing these bats to aggressively chase counting stats, with **Jacob Wilson** (64.31) providing additional value in the lead-off spot thanks to favorable park factors, despite the tougher test against Payton Tolle.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Curtis Mead** on the bench. Despite a solid score of 55.09 and a significant 10% park boost, the optimizer favored the floor provided by **Wade Meckler** and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Curtis Mead** projected well, the potential for high-impact stolen base contributions from our starters, particularly in the lower-order spots, kept him out of the primary lineup. We are maintaining caution with **Sam Antonacci**, whose score of 45.46 is suppressed by a tough L/L matchup against Max Fried; he remains the pivot point if we need to rotate in **Miguel Vargas** or **Coby Mayo** once official lineups confirm the depth of our bench options.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters. While **Drake Baldwin** is currently tracking for a 62.85 score at the top of the order, any shuffle in the lineup card could shift his efficiency. Furthermore, while **Luis Lara** carries a modest 49.07, he is active primarily for his speed profile, supported by a 5% wind boost that could turn fly balls into production. We are closely monitoring weather reports for any late-breaking wind 